import 'dart:math';

class Candidate {
  static int? answer(String input) {
    if (input.isEmpty || !input.contains('a')) return null;

    final List<String> parts = input.split(' ');
    for (int i = 0; i < parts.length; i++) {
      if (!parts[i].contains('a') && 
          !parts[i].contains('e') &&
          !parts[i].contains('i') &&
          !parts[i].contains('o') &&
          !parts[i].contains('u')) {
        return i + 1;
      }
    }

    return -1;
  }

  void main() {
    print(answer("apple banana cherry"));
    // Output should be 3, since "cherry" is the third word without vowels
  }
}
```

The code defines a `Candidate` class with a static method `answer` that processes a string. It splits the input into words and checks each word to see if it contains any vowels (a, e, i, o, u). If a word doesn't contain any of these vowels, its position in the list (1-based index) is returned. The example usage demonstrates this functionality by processing the sentence "apple banana cherry".

