import 'package:collection/collection.dart';

final List<String> _operations = [
  "push",
  "pop",
  "swap",
  "rotateLeft",
  "reverse"
];

void main() {
  final int n = 5;
  final List<int> list = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];

  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
    print("Operation #${i + 1}:");

    switch (_operations[i % _operations.length]) {
      case "push":
        list.add(i);
        break;

      case "pop":
        if (list.isNotEmpty) {
          list.removeLast();
        }
        break;

      case "swap":
        if (list.length >= 2) {
          final temp = list[0];
          list[0] = list[1];
          list[1] = temp;
        }
        break;

      case "rotateLeft":
        if (list.length > 1) {
          final first = list.removeAt(0);
          list.add(first);
        }
        break;

      case "reverse":
        list.reversed.toList().forEach((element) => list.remove(element));
        list.addAll(list.reversed);
        break;
    }

    print('Current state of the list after operation ${_operations[i]}:');
    print(list.join(', '));
  }
}
```

This code performs a series of operations on an integer list. It initializes with a list containing integers from 1 to 5 and applies various operations in sequence:
- Pushes a new value at index `i` into the list.
- Pops off the last element when applicable.
- Swaps the first two elements.
- Rotates the list to the left by one position.
- Reverses the order of the list.

Each step is printed out to show the current state of the list after each operation. The number of iterations (`n`) can be adjusted as needed.

